content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22300.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow is reported approximately 20% lower over two weeks at unchanged valve settings, so the manual's low-flow/head troubleshooting applies. The only documented numerical flow reference is rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m; this is not an allowable percentage-drop limit. An absolute current flow or compliance with a flow acceptance band cannot be determined without the baseline and operating point.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Using the applicable HF-300 bearing-housing vibration-velocity chart, the numerical value 2.0 mm/s lies in Zone A, 0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary. It is below the Zone C restricted range and Zone D damage/stop range. Classification is provisional until the reading is confirmed as RMS velocity and as the highest reading from both bearing housings, as required by the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing-housing temperature limits apply because the manual specifies temperature measurement on the housing surface. Provided the reported 65 C is that measurement, it is within the normal range up to 70 C: 5 C below the normal limit, 15 C below the 80 C alarm, and 25 C below the 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage is reported, so the manual's leakage-at-shaft-seal symptom is not presently supported. The service bulletin nevertheless governs seal selection for any replacement because of this pump's serial number; it does not by itself prove that the installed seal has failed or explain the flow loss.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 planned corrective investigation is appropriate on the available evidence: there is a material low-flow symptom, but the reported temperature is below alarm/trip limits and the numerical vibration reading is not in a restricted or stop zone. No immediate-stop condition is documented by these readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller, with wear-ring condition also requiring inspection: this is the first listed probable cause and inspection action for low flow or head.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in the suction: the manual lists this as a probable cause of low flow or head and directs venting of the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A closed valve: this remains a documented possible cause, although it is lower in the check order because the report says valve settings have not changed; verify rather than assume.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, record the actual baseline and current flow and head at the reported settings and verify valve position. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and record the bearing-housing surface temperature for comparison with 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Confirm that the 2.0 mm/s report is an RMS bearing-housing measurement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check for the documented closed-valve cause and vent the casing to address possible air in suction, then reassess flow. Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If these checks do not resolve the low flow, isolate and drain the pump before mechanical disassembly. Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; its design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the impeller and wear rings and record their condition and any available measurements. If impeller replacement is authorised after inspection, the identified impeller is HF3-210, 5-vane, 330 mm. Do not invent wear rejection limits: none are supplied. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket on reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not automatically diagnose seal failure solely from the bulletin or the flow complaint. If mechanical-seal replacement is separately required or authorised, remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Fit HF3-450B, not HF3-450, with a new casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; tighten its seal gland nut to 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 only when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth under the stated bulletin criterion. Obtain Table 5 for any other fastener torques rather than applying 30 Nm indiscriminately.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Limits are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angularity.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During recommissioning, preserve seal flush and avoid dry running. Record final flow and head, inspect for leakage, repeat bearing-housing vibration and surface-temperature checks, and classify the highest vibration reading. Demonstrate recovery against the measured pre-fault baseline; do not treat 300 m3/h at 45 m as an acceptance value unless the pump is actually tested at that rated duty point.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; one required whenever the casing is opened, including reassembly after mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-210",
      "description": "Conditional impeller, 5-vane, 330 mm; supply only if inspection establishes that impeller replacement is required and replacement is authorised.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Conditional pre-set cartridge mechanical seal for any seal replacement on serial HF3-22300. It supersedes HF3-450 for this serial range; gland nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve; replace if inspection finds scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before the documented back pull-out/mechanical-seal disassembly sequence.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge; never run the pump dry, including during troubleshooting and recommissioning.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For continued condition monitoring, measure vibration weekly on both bearing housings and act on the highest reading. Zone C is restricted operation requiring planned maintenance; apply the Figure 3 instruction to stop the pump whenever a reading is classified in Zone D, where damage is likely.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply the bearing-housing surface-temperature limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Initial field-technician diagnostic labour covers verification of operating readings and valve condition, casing venting, flow reassessment, and bearing-housing vibration/temperature checks. No labour duration is documented.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical disassembly and reassembly labour covers back pull-out access, impeller/wear-ring inspection and any authorised impeller or seal work; include lifting equipment for the 68 kg assembly. No crew size or hours are specified in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser-alignment labour is required after any work moving the motor or bearing housing, using the documented offset and angular tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: the generic manual parts list identifies HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 and requires HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-112 is serial HF3-22300 and therefore falls within the bulletin range. For this asset, the bulletin governs any replacement: use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-setting and torque resolution: the general manual procedure says to inspect the sleeve and tighten fasteners to Table 5. For this in-range serial, the more specific bulletin states that HF3-450B is pre-set, requires no sleeve measurement for seal setting, and uses a 30 Nm gland-nut torque instead of the former 25 Nm. Apply 30 Nm only to the HF3-450B gland nut, retain the sleeve scoring inspection, and use the bulletin's replacement threshold of scoring exceeding 0.1 mm. Table 5 is not supplied for other fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What are the measured pre-fault and current flow and head, and at what suction/discharge operating conditions? The evidence provides rated duty but no permissible flow-drop percentage or post-repair flow tolerance.",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration value measured as RMS velocity on a bearing housing, at which housing, and was it the highest of both required measurement locations?",
    "Was the 65 C reading taken on the bearing-housing surface as specified, and which bearing housing did it represent?",
    "What are the impeller and wear-ring inspection measurements, wear rejection limits, clearances and wear-ring part number? The supplied evidence requires inspection but provides none of these criteria or a wear-ring part number.",
    "What are the complete Table 5 fastener torques? Only the HF3-450B gland-nut torque of 30 Nm is available in the supplied evidence.",
    "Which seal is currently installed, has the HF3-450B conversion already been completed, and is a proactive seal conversion intended? The bulletin controls replacement-part selection but does not explicitly require immediate replacement of a non-leaking installed seal.",
    "If the pump is disassembled, what is the measured shaft-sleeve scoring depth? The conditional sleeve-replacement decision cannot be made before inspection."
  ]
}
